F=[
("a-f026","a","The fifth Global Biodiversity Outlook found that none of the 20 Aichi Targets was fully achieved globally by 2020, although six were partially achieved.","Fifth Global Biodiversity Outlook ప్రకారం 2020 నాటికి 20 Aichi Targetsలో ఒక్కటీ globalగా fully achieve కాలేదు; అయితే ఆరు partially achieve అయ్యాయి.",["src-cbd-gbf"]),
("a-f027","a","KMGBF Target 19 seeks at least US$200 billion per year from all sources by 2030. Within it, international biodiversity finance to developing countries should reach at least US$20 billion yearly by 2025 and US$30 billion yearly by 2030.","KMGBF Target 19 ప్రకారం 2030 నాటికి అన్ని sources నుంచి సంవత్సరానికి కనీసం US$200 billion mobilize చేయాలి. ఇందులో developing countriesకు international biodiversity finance 2025 నాటికి US$20 billion, 2030 నాటికి US$30 billion yearly చేరాలి.",["src-cbd-gbf"]),
("a-f028","a","Under Nagoya, PIC is required where the provider country's domestic ABS law requires it; MAT arrange benefit-sharing. The Protocol also addresses traditional knowledge associated with genetic resources and relevant community rights under domestic law.","Nagoya కింద provider country domestic ABS law కోరినప్పుడు PIC అవసరం; MAT benefit-sharingను arrange చేస్తాయి. Genetic resourcesకు సంబంధించిన traditional knowledge, domestic law కింద community rightsను కూడా Protocol address చేస్తుంది.",["src-cbd-protocols"]),
("b-f016","b","Ramsar's wise-use obligation applies to all wetlands in a Party's territory, not only Ramsar Sites. The Convention was adopted on 2 February 1971, the date observed as World Wetlands Day, and entered into force on 21 December 1975.","Ramsar wise-use obligation Party territoryలోని అన్ని wetlandsకు వర్తిస్తుంది; Ramsar Sitesకే కాదు. Convention 2 February 1971న adopt అయింది—ఆ తేదీ World Wetlands Day—మరియు 21 December 1975న forceలోకి వచ్చింది.",["src-ramsar-official"]),
("c-f012","c","World Heritage inscription requires Outstanding Universal Value, at least one of ten criteria, and adequate protection and management. The Committee will not consider a nomination unless the property is already on the State Party's Tentative List.","World Heritage inscriptionకు Outstanding Universal Value, ten criteriaలో కనీసం ఒకటి, adequate protection-management అవసరం. Property State Party Tentative Listలో లేకపోతే Committee nominationను consider చేయదు.",["src-unesco-world-heritage-criteria"]),
("d-f010","d","India signed the BBNJ Agreement on 25 September 2024. In the UN Treaty Collection record checked for the lesson draft, India had not deposited ratification; this dynamic status must be rechecked because signature, ratification and becoming a Party are distinct stages.","India BBNJ Agreementపై 25 September 2024న sign చేసింది. Lesson draft కోసం check చేసిన UN Treaty Collection recordలో ratification deposit చేయలేదు; signature, ratification, Party కావడం వేర్వేరు stages కాబట్టి ఈ dynamic statusను recheck చేయాలి.",["src-unct-bbnj-status-india"]),
("d-f011","d","BBNJ Article 52 provides a financial mechanism comprising a voluntary trust fund, a special fund and the GEF Trust Fund. These related components are not one interchangeable fund.","BBNJ Article 52 financial mechanismలో voluntary trust fund, special fund, GEF Trust Fund ఉంటాయి. ఇవి related components; ఒకే interchangeable fund కావు.",["src-un-bbnj-official","src-gef-conventions-and-funds"]),
]
